#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:5
#: 83c749418f91419da11bf87e46386347
msgid "Submitting Patches Back to Master"
msgstr "向 Master 提交补丁"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:10
#: 7670244b3af24c26bdf66e53b1c36a97
msgid ""
"*Before* working on a new patch search for existing related pull requests, "
"and check for linked pull requests in the issue you're planning to fix. If "
"someone is already working on the problem you can review/test their "
"submission and join the discussion thread instead of creating your own "
"submission."
msgstr ""
"在开始编写新补丁 *之前*，请先搜索现有的相关 pull request，并检查您计划修复的 issue 中链接的 pull "
"request。如果已有人在处理该问题，您可以评审/测试其提交并加入讨论帖，而不是另行创建自己的提交。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:12
#: 06117d5781a343d78f616bc845e5ff47
msgid ""
"Once you have a bug fix or new feature you would like to have included in "
"the ArduPilot project you should submit a `Pull Request "
"<https://help.github.com/articles/about-pull-requests/>`__. The main "
"developers will see your changes in the `Pulls list, "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/pulls>`__ review them and if all "
"goes well they will be merged into master."
msgstr ""
"当您有需要纳入 ArduPilot 项目的 Bug 修复或新功能时，应提交 `PR（合并请求） "
"<https://help.github.com/articles/about-pull-requests/>`__。主要开发者将在 `PR 列表 "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/pulls>`__ 中看到您的变更，经过审查后，如果一切顺利将被合并到 "
"master。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:17
#: 443cc6ff1e5c4dccaf89f227c5302c8e
msgid "This page provides advice to make the process go smoothly."
msgstr "本页面提供使流程顺利进行的建议。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:20
#: f308f2e414b94f69bf0b98ec2cc907bb
msgid "Preparing commits"
msgstr "准备提交"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:22
#: 2059b4d7af7a467485b8e412a6045123
msgid ""
"Commits should be **in a new branch** of your :ref:`fork <git-"
"fork>`/:ref:`clone <git-clone>` (i.e. not \"master\"). These should be done "
"on a local branch and then pushed to your web-based fork of ArduPilot."
msgstr ""
"提交应 **在新分支** 中进行，位于您 :ref:`fork <git-fork>`/:ref:`clone <git-clone>` 的仓库中（即非"
" master 分支）。应在本地分支上提交，再推送到您在 GitHub 上的 ArduPilot fork。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:24
#: 1d05b8128b714ce481f2ce1ec613e05d
msgid ""
"The new branch should be :ref:`up-to-date <git-rebase>` with "
"`ArduPilot/master <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__  and should "
"not include any other changes."
msgstr ""
"新分支应与 `ArduPilot/master <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__ "
":ref:`保持同步 <git-rebase>`，且不应包含任何其他变更。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:26
#: fcac955412f34930be115ea9e51c17e9
msgid ""
"**Commits should be small and do just one thing.** If a change touches "
"multiple libraries then there should be a separate commit per library, and a"
" separate commit per vehicle directory. This is true even if it means that "
"intermediate commits break the build. This also implies that moving code "
"from one library to another happens in two commits: one that \"deletes\" it "
"from the old spot, and a separate one that \"creates\" it at the new spot. "
"It's better for unrelated changes in a single library to be separate commits"
" in the pull request."
msgstr ""
"**提交应小而专一，每次只做一件事。** "
"如果变更涉及多个库，则每个库应有单独的提交，每个飞行器目录也应有单独的提交。即使这意味着中间提交会破坏构建，也应如此。这也意味着将代码从一个库移到另一个库需要两个提交：一个从原位置「删除」它，另一个在新位置「创建」它。对于单个库中互不相关的变更，最好在"
" pull request 中拆分为单独的提交。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:35
#: 16c16bf9f964409e8cdea7411149cc1b
msgid ""
"Do not create 'only fix formatting' commits. The disruption they cause to "
"git history is more significant than their improvement to the code."
msgstr "不要创建「仅修复格式」的提交。它们对 git 历史造成的干扰大于其对代码的改进。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:38
#: 2cc6ef26eb884915b83a8dbe533537a6
msgid ""
"Only add \"high value\" comments to existing code. Comments disrupt the git "
"history, and the code should already be written clearly enough to describe "
"what it does. Be prepared to explain/defend the importance of any new "
"comments to reviewers, and defer to their judgement to resolve any "
"disagreement over a comment's value. Comments should not explain \"what\" "
"code does, they explain \"why\" (or perhaps \"how\" in a clever-but-"
"difficult implementation)."
msgstr ""
"只为现有代码添加「高价值」的注释。注释会干扰 git "
"历史，而且代码本身就应写得足够清晰，能够说明其作用。请准备好向评审者解释/论证任何新注释的重要性，如对注释的价值有分歧，请以评审者的判断为准。注释不应解释代码「做什么」，而应解释「为什么」（或者在巧妙但难懂的实现中解释「如何做」）。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:46
#: 202495d70e6242ea851ec9c6d7fb40dc
msgid ""
"Resist moving code within files/libraries. Preserving the in-file location "
"of code is preferred over rearranging the file(s) to improve organization. "
"Defer to a reviewer's judgement to resolve any disagreements regarding this."
msgstr "尽量避免在文件/库内移动代码。保持代码在文件中的原有位置优先于为改善组织结构而重排文件。如有分歧，请以评审者的判断为准。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:51
#: 5521c01b181345b69bc8cef29bf52c1b
msgid "Do not clean up whitespace, unless you are already changing the lines."
msgstr "不要清理空白字符，除非您本来就要修改这些行。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:53
#: 969b9fc8212f4cb9b263d85db3234550
msgid "**Well-written, concise comments** are encouraged."
msgstr "鼓励 **简洁、清晰的注释**。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:55
#: de29fe6ba5d64dd1ba03587d2248e59b
msgid "Commit messages should be of the form:"
msgstr "提交信息应遵循以下格式："

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:63
#: 2af081a5866a453a9c31c25e55c03765
msgid "Example:"
msgstr "示例："

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:71
#: 6f701a6e8ad94e3487e2106f6c8e8c7e
msgid ""
"The brief description (summary) line should be less than 72 characters so it"
" renders correctly in Github."
msgstr "简要描述（摘要）行应少于 72 个字符，以便在 Github 上正确显示。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:73
#: c44304ddd926431a8b94d5b18814306b
msgid ""
"**clean up your local commit history** :ref:`using interactive rebase <git-"
"interactive-rebase>` (i.e. ``git rebase -i \"HEAD~10\"``) to re-arrange "
"patches and fold things together. The idea is to present a logical set of "
"patches for review. It can take a bit of effort to get used to interactive "
"rebase, but it is definitely worth learning. Refer to `online resources "
"<http://gitready.com/advanced/2009/02/10/squashing-commits-with-"
"rebase.html>`__ to understand how to use this tool. Also see this video: "
"https://youtu.be/iMUWQUD_Rsg"
msgstr ""
"**使用** :ref:`交互式 rebase <git-interactive-rebase>` **整理本地提交历史** （即 ``git "
"rebase -i \"HEAD~10\"``），重新排列补丁并合并相关提交，以便向审查者呈现一组逻辑清晰的补丁。掌握交互式 rebase "
"可能需要一些时间，但绝对值得学习。请参阅 `在线资料 "
"<http://gitready.com/advanced/2009/02/10/squashing-commits-with-"
"rebase.html>`__ 了解如何使用该工具，以及视频：https://youtu.be/iMUWQUD_Rsg"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:80
#: 3d2da793e05a4a74a415bbcb3b422573
msgid ""
"Each commit should involve only a single library. The commits of the changes"
" in each library should be squashed (see :ref:`git-interactive-rebase`) into"
" the minimal number of commits per library that allows readability and "
"clarity when reviewing (usually only one commit). The \"Tools/gittools/git-"
"subsystems-split\" script can be run on any commit spanning multiple "
"libraries to create a single commit for each library module affected before "
"submitting. if needed."
msgstr ""
"每次提交应只涉及一个库。每个库内的变更提交应使用 squash（参见 :ref:`git-interactive-"
"rebase`）合并为最少数量的提交，以确保审查时的可读性和清晰度（通常每个库只有一个提交）。必要时，可在提交前对跨多个库的提交运行「Tools/gittools/git-"
"subsystems-split」脚本，为每个受影响的库模块创建单独的提交。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:82
#: b810193728384427a8f0f02c9a29979a
msgid ""
"Do not submit patches with commented-out code or code that is never "
"reachable within ``#define`` s."
msgstr "不要提交带有注释掉的代码或 ``#define`` 中永远无法到达的代码。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:84
#: 4cf0b6353ed24bfe96a606b6a06cdc3f
msgid ""
"Do not include git merge commits in your commit history; :ref:`rebase <git-"
"rebase>`  your branch on the master branch, do not ``git pull`` changes in."
msgstr ""
"不要在提交历史中包含 git 合并提交；应对您的分支进行 :ref:`rebase <git-rebase>` 到 master 分支，而非使用 "
"``git pull`` 引入变更。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:86
#: 8408c81100194b94a3e91fc3d6164fd6
msgid ""
"Do not include any git ``fixup!`` commits in your PR; these are only ever "
"supposed to be a temporary part of a git workflow"
msgstr "不要在 PR 中包含任何 git ``fixup!`` 提交；这类提交仅应是 git 工作流中的临时部分。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:88
#: 02bba1b5fdd146e7a571bdd1acc74837
msgid ""
"Try to follow the :ref:`style guide <style-guide>` so your code fits in with"
" the existing code. In particular, ensure your editor uses 4 spaces instead "
"of tabs."
msgstr ""
"请尽量遵循 :ref:`代码风格指南 <style-guide>`，使您的代码与现有代码保持一致。特别注意确保您的编辑器使用 4 个空格而非制表符。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:91
#: a991fad8e4314c22aba51eba32edb731
msgid ""
"For Python changes follow the :ref:`style guide <python-style-guide>` so "
"your code fits in with the existing code."
msgstr "对于 Python 改动，请遵循 :ref:`代码风格指南 <python-style-guide>`，使您的代码与现有代码保持一致。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:93
#: 630c3cb043854b41a68b06652fea7b37
msgid ""
"Unix line endings (LF) are used. Git should take care of this automatically,"
" but if you notice that you have a lot of files that show up as changed in "
"``git status`` but you didn't touch those files, you may need to `check to "
"see if local git settings regarding line endings are correct "
"<https://help.github.com/articles/dealing-with-line-endings>`__."
msgstr ""
"使用 Unix 行尾（LF）。git 通常会自动处理，但如果您注意到 ``git status`` 显示大量未经修改的文件发生了变更，可能需要 "
"`检查本地 git 行尾设置是否正确 <https://help.github.com/articles/dealing-with-line-"
"endings>`__。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:99
#: 390c759773bc4e859d165644cae85b58
msgid ""
"read your changes, doing your own review. The best way to do this is to use "
"the \"gitk\" tool. Look over your own changes critically. Make sure they do "
"not include anything you don't want to go into the pull request. It is best "
"to read your changes at least several hours after you wrote the code, and "
"preferably the next day. Look over them carefully and look for any bugs."
msgstr ""
"请仔细阅读自己的变更，进行自我审查。最佳方式是使用「gitk」工具。批判性地审视自己的变更，确保其中不包含不希望进入 PR "
"的内容。最好在编写代码至少数小时后（最好是第二天）再审阅，仔细检查并查找任何 Bug。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:106
#: e0049a66faa64d2f96b29b29a391ca66
msgid ""
"if you have access to a Linux build environment then build your modified "
"tree using `Tools/scripts/build_all.sh "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/scripts/build_all.sh>`__."
" That will test that all the builds for different boards and vehicle types "
"work. If you don't have a Linux build environment then please test the build"
" for Pixhawk boards and rover, copter and plane if your changes may affect "
"those vehicles."
msgstr ""
"如果您有 Linux 构建环境，请使用 `Tools/scripts/build_all.sh "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/scripts/build_all.sh>`__"
" 测试您修改后的代码树，以验证不同板型和飞行器类型的构建均可正常工作。如果没有 Linux 构建环境，请至少测试 Pixhawk "
"板型的构建，以及如果您的变更可能影响 Rover、Copter 和 Plane 的话，也请测试这些飞行器。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:114
#: dfc69fe8dd494e0c9e5c88d9b5a9f053
msgid ""
"test your changes in :ref:`SITL <sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop>` if "
"possible. If you can't run SITL then test your changes in a real vehicle."
msgstr ""
"如有可能，在 :ref:`SITL <sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop>` 中测试您的变更。若无法运行 "
"SITL，请在真实飞行器上测试。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:118
#: 6dbd668aa12942d7aa423da5a85413a8
msgid "Submitting a pull request"
msgstr "提交 PR"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:120
#: ce2425975de94f1cab41a4507b5dcf39
msgid ""
"To submit a `pull request on GitHub <https://help.github.com/articles/using-"
"pull-requests>`__ for review and possible inclusion in the official "
"repository, follow these directions:"
msgstr ""
"要在 GitHub 上 `提交 PR <https://help.github.com/articles/using-pull-requests>`__"
" 以供审查并可能纳入官方仓库，请按以下步骤操作："

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:123
#: 41f8a68b02204387affa7dec0dbbd5c7
msgid ""
"Open your :ref:`fork <git-fork>` on the GitHub web page select the branch "
"from the drop-down and then push the \"New Pull Request\" button"
msgstr ""
"在 GitHub 网页上打开您的 :ref:`fork <git-fork>`，从下拉菜单选择分支，然后点击「New Pull Request」按钮。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:129
#: 8c44aa87efaf4e019c9e91ccef78f838
msgid ""
"Check the \"base fork\" is `ArduPilot/ardupilot "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__ and \"base\" is \"master\" and "
"then fill in the PR's subject line and detailed description.  The detailed "
"description should include any evidence of testing performed."
msgstr ""
"确认「base fork」为 `ArduPilot/ardupilot "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__，「base」为「master」，然后填写 PR "
"的标题和详细描述，描述中应包含所有已进行测试的证据。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:131
#: d8a926e1204b4546843c850ccc66e57f
msgid ""
"Check the list of changes at the bottom of the page only includes your "
"intended changes, then push the \"Create pull request\" button."
msgstr "确认页面底部的变更列表仅包含您预期的变更，然后点击「Create pull request」按钮。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:139
#: f405b70e498143bcb3f4bd9d177f9b0f
msgid "Next Steps"
msgstr "后续步骤"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:141
#: a74dc428668340eabc517c56382108d8
msgid ""
"You can track the state of your PR from the `Pull Requests list "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/pulls>`__."
msgstr ""
"您可以在 `PR 列表 <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/pulls>`__ 中跟踪 PR 状态。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:143
#: 2fae9785c1bf4e37b15437948731832b
msgid "PRs are more likely to be merged quickly if:"
msgstr "以下情况下 PR 更容易被快速合并："

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:145
#: 7756c1013d1d4bfd942f90778aa29081
msgid "The PR clearly states what changes in behaviour are expected"
msgstr "PR 清晰说明了预期的行为变化"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:146
#: fa6361b581a54bd0b4f3d6ec4599073f
msgid ""
"Good testing evidence is provided.  This could be graphs of logs recorded "
"before and after the change, possibly from a :ref:`simulation "
"<simulation-2>`. Check for existing :ref:`autotests <the-ardupilot-autotest-"
"framework>`, and update them if they get broken by the change. Add new ones "
"to cover new functionality you're introducing, or bug fixes presently not "
"tested, if you are capable."
msgstr ""
"提供充分的测试证据。这可以是变更前后记录的日志图表，也可以来自 :ref:`仿真 <simulation-2>`。请检查现有的 :ref:`自动测试 "
"<the-ardupilot-autotest-framework>`，如果它们被变更破坏，请更新它们。如有能力，请为您引入的新功能或当前尚未测试的 "
"bug 修复添加新测试。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:147
#: 21ab2d87fda14b00a685670c336b3285
msgid "Code follows the :ref:`style guide <style-guide>`"
msgstr "代码遵循 :ref:`代码风格指南 <style-guide>`"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:148
#: 075cdf2eebd745c78d927a1336698f2c
msgid "Python code follows the :ref:`python style guide <python-style-guide>`"
msgstr "Python 代码遵循 :ref:`Python 代码风格指南 <python-style-guide>`"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:149
#: 8f94aef112c44b19b5d283ac9993691c
msgid ""
"Each commit in the PR affects only one subsystem and the commit title is "
"prefixed with the subsystem name (e.g. \"AP_GPS: correct uBlox logging "
"parameter descriptions\").  The `Tools/gittools/git-subsystems-split "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/gittools/git-"
"subsystems-split>`__ script may be useful for this"
msgstr ""
"PR 中每次提交只影响一个子系统，且提交标题以子系统名称为前缀（例如「AP_GPS: correct uBlox logging parameter "
"descriptions」）。可使用 `Tools/gittools/git-subsystems-split "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/gittools/git-"
"subsystems-split>`__ 脚本辅助完成。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:150
#: 4cefbb549d664021b5a2cabd7d2de751
msgid ""
"PR passes all automated CI tests.  CI tests sometimes fail for reason "
"unrelated to your PR (e.g. dependency failures, \"flapping tests\").  Please"
" force push the PR to re-run the tests"
msgstr ""
"PR 通过了所有自动化 CI 测试。CI 测试有时会因与 PR 无关的原因失败（如依赖失败、「不稳定测试」）。请强制推送 PR 以重新运行测试。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:151
#: 81328f494d634e09966414de22db3ef8
msgid ""
"The PR is discussed on one of the :ref:`weekly dev calls <ardupilot-discord-"
"server>`.  To get the PR discussed add the \"DevCallTopic\" or \"DevCallEU\""
" label.  If you are unable to add the label ping one of the core developers "
"on `ArduPilot Discord <https://ardupilot.org/discord>`__ (see the \"code-"
"review\" channel).  \"Core developers\" can be identified by the \"dev-"
"team\" badge in Discord and some also appear as `top contributors in Github "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/graphs/contributors>`__"
msgstr ""
"PR 在 :ref:`每周开发者会议 <ardupilot-discord-server>` 之一中被讨论。要让 PR "
"得到讨论，请添加「DevCallTopic」或「DevCallEU」标签。如果您无法添加标签，请在 `ArduPilot Discord "
"<https://ardupilot.org/discord>`__ 的「code-review」频道中联系某位核心开发者。「核心开发者」可通过 "
"Discord 中的「dev-team」徽章识别，部分人员也出现在 `Github 贡献者排行榜 "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/graphs/contributors>`__ 中。"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:153
#: 8d7bf7cfd7d24a749f5861af0e3ca859
msgid ""
"It is very common, especially for large changes, for the core developers to "
"ask you to modify the pull request to fit in better with the existing code "
"base or resolve some knock-on impact that you may not have known about. "
"Please don't take this the wrong way, we're definitely not trying to make "
"your life difficult!"
msgstr "对于大型变更，核心开发者很常要求您修改 PR 以更好地融入现有代码库，或解决您可能未知的连带影响。请不要误解，我们绝对不是要为难您！"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:155
#: 08517baf8df345d38e29e1a33a0e4172
msgid ""
"If your PR gets stuck please understand that this is likely just because "
"ArduPilot receives a lot of code contributions and it is difficult for the "
"core dev team to review and merge them all.  Here's some advice to get a PR "
"\"unstuck\":"
msgstr ""
"如果您的 PR 陷入停滞，请理解这很可能只是因为 ArduPilot 收到了大量代码贡献，核心开发团队难以及时审查和合并所有内容。以下是一些让 "
"PR「解除停滞」的建议："

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:157
#: fff1d6ce280e41f99e788c06eed5c82f
msgid ""
"Review the advice above titled \"PRs are more likely to be merged quickly "
"if\""
msgstr "重新阅读上述「PR 更容易被快速合并的情况」"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:158
#: a468d2edca8d447cadcf33a6fb85b124
msgid ""
"Attend one of the two :ref:`weekly dev calls <ardupilot-discord-server>`"
msgstr "参加两场 :ref:`每周开发者会议 <ardupilot-discord-server>` 之一"

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:159
#: 306e1ca5cd9e48109e0d90cc4f011128
msgid ""
"Send a note to a \"core developer\" in the code-review channel.  These can "
"be identified by the \"dev-team\" badge in Discord and some also appear as "
"`top contributors in Github "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/graphs/contributors>`__"
msgstr ""
"在 code-review 频道给某位「核心开发者」发消息。可通过 Discord 中的「dev-team」徽章识别，部分人员也出现在 `Github "
"贡献者排行榜 <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/graphs/contributors>`__ 中。"

